# Lock-screen wallpaper: points KScreenLocker's own real greeter wallpaper
# plugin at one of this project's own wallpapers (packages/kuura-assets,
# design/generate_wallpapers.py) instead of leaving it on whatever stock
# default the "org.kde.image" plugin falls back to. Installed to
# /etc/skel/.config/kscreenlockerrc by the kuura-shell package
# (docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md) - a per-user default a user can still change
# through System Settings afterwards, the same role every other file in
# this directory plays.
#
# SCOPE (a deliberate, documented limitation, not an oversight - Vaihe 6 of
# the working brief, "Sovellustason viimeistely", the lock-screen sub-task):
# no bespoke lock-screen QML ships in this project. The project owner was
# shown the real trade-off and explicitly chose the smaller option: forking
# the lock screen's own QML would mean forking Plasma's entire "Plasma/
# Shell" KPackage (panels/desktop layout included - unlike "Plasma/
# LookAndFeel", which packages/kuura-lookandfeel/ already uses for the
# logout dialog, Plasma/Shell has no per-component fallback), a much bigger
# blast radius for one small cosmetic touch. This file ships only a branded
# default wallpaper through the lock screen's own real config keys below,
# and relies on the lock screen's own existing, confirmed-free colour
# inheritance for everything else: KDE's own real LockScreenUi.qml sets
# `Kirigami.Theme.colorSet: Kirigami.Theme.Complementary`, so the unlock
# text/avatar there already follow the active colour scheme with no file of
# ours needed for that part.
#
# REAL CONFIG KEYS (confirmed live against the pinned kscreenlocker 6.7.5-1
# / plasma-workspace 6.7.5-1 source at invent.kde.org, git tag v6.7.5,
# cross-checked against a real distro's own shipped kscreenlockerrc and
# KDE's own plasma-apply-wallpaperimage.cpp - not guessed):
#   - [Greeter] WallpaperPlugin=org.kde.image - the real KConfigXT entry
#     (kscreenlocker's settings/kscreenlockersettings.kcfg:
#     `<entry name="wallpaperPluginId" key="WallpaperPlugin"><default>
#     org.kde.image</default></entry>`), read by the greeter
#     (greeterapp.cpp: `m_wallpaperPackage.setPath(KScreenSaverSettingsBase
#     ::self()->wallpaperPluginId())`) to decide which wallpaper KPackage to
#     load. "org.kde.image" is already the real default, so this line is a
#     no-op on a stock install - kept here only to make the choice explicit
#     and because the group below depends on its exact value as a group name.
#   - [Greeter][Wallpaper][org.kde.image][General] Image=<file:// URL> - the
#     real nested KConfigXT group a loaded "org.kde.image" wallpaper
#     package's own config reads (plasma-workspace's wallpapers/image/
#     imagepackage/contents/config/main.xml: group "General", entry "Image",
#     type String). The nesting itself is confirmed directly against
#     shutdowndlg.cpp's real group-building code,
#     `sharedConfig()->group("Greeter").group("Wallpaper").group(
#     wallpaperPluginId())`. The value format (a literal "file://<path>"
#     string, not a bare filesystem path) is confirmed against KDE's own
#     wallpapers/image/plasma-apply-wallpaperimage.cpp, which builds exactly
#     `d.writeConfig('Image', 'file://<path>');` (its own source:
#     `u"d.writeConfig('Image', 'file://" + wallpaperFile + u"');"`) when
#     setting this same key for the desktop wallpaper picker.
#   - FillMode is deliberately left UNSET here (keeps the wallpaper plugin's
#     own real default, FillMode=2 in the same main.xml) - this project has
#     no documented reason yet to override how the image is cropped/scaled,
#     matching the "ship only the one real lever this task needs" discipline
#     design/generators/sddm_theme.py's own module docstring already uses.
#
# WALLPAPER CHOICE: design/generate_wallpapers.py's own "radial-glow"
# composition, dark mode. Picked over the other four compositions because
# its centred glow fades out towards every edge, leaving calm, low-contrast
# corners wherever LockScreenUi.qml actually places the clock/avatar/
# password field (which this project does not control - see SCOPE above);
# the edge-to-edge two-stop gradients ("vertical-dawn", "diagonal-drift",
# "banded-horizon") risk a bright or busy patch landing directly behind that
# text depending on screen resolution/DPI. Dark mode (not light) matches
# this project's own SDDM greeter's fixed-dark choice
# (design/generate_sddm.py's own module docstring) for the same underlying
# reason: a surface that cannot react to the active session's own light/
# dark toggle reads most consistently as one deliberately fixed, high-
# contrast choice. Both picks are real product/design calls, not technical
# requirements discovered by research - flagged explicitly in this change's
# own handback/report.
#
# HARD-CODED "kuura" IN THE PATH BELOW, NOT ${DISTRO_NAME} - a deliberate
# deviation, flagged explicitly in this change's own handback/report: this
# file is installed as a plain, static skel file (one `install -Dm644` line
# in packages/kuura-shell/PKGBUILD's own package(), the same pattern as this
# directory's kwinrc/kglobalshortcutsrc/kdeglobals/krunnerrc - no sed
# templating step, unlike kvantum.kvconfig.in/settings.ini.in in this same
# directory), while the real wallpaper path below is genuinely
# ${DISTRO_NAME}-dependent: packages/kuura-assets/PKGBUILD installs it under
# /usr/share/backgrounds/${DISTRO_NAME}/${DISTRO_NAME}-radial-glow-dark.png.
# For this project's own real deployment DISTRO_NAME is "kuura", so the two
# values coincide today; if DISTRO_NAME is ever changed, this file must be
# updated by hand (or converted into a kscreenlockerrc.in template with its
# own sed step) or the lock screen will silently fall back to no custom
# wallpaper (a missing Image path is not a crash, just an unbranded default -
# the same "no package, no crash" failure mode kdeglobals' own
# LookAndFeelPackage key documents for a missing kuura-lookandfeel package).
[Greeter]
WallpaperPlugin=org.kde.image

[Greeter][Wallpaper][org.kde.image][General]
Image=file:///usr/share/backgrounds/kuura/kuura-radial-glow-dark.png
